cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these benchmarks, please cite this repository. An archived Zenodo release with a DOI is planned."
title: "Edge AI LLM Inference Benchmarking on T3 Gemstone O1 and Arduino UNO Q"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sucu
    given-names: Ali Haydar
repository-code: "https://github.com/alihaydarsucu/t3-gemstone-benchmark"
url: "https://github.com/alihaydarsucu/t3-gemstone-benchmark"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/alihaydarsucu/t3-gemstone-benchmark/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
abstract: >-
  Reproducible edge-AI LLM inference benchmarks using llama.cpp on the T3
  Gemstone O1 (TI AM67A) and the Arduino UNO Q (Qualcomm QRB2210). The project
  measures prompt-processing and token-generation throughput across
  quantization levels, thread counts, and CPU/Vulkan backends, together with
  perplexity, task accuracy, memory use, and thermal behaviour. The current
  dataset is preliminary and incomplete; see the README for the exact status.
keywords:
  - edge AI
  - LLM inference
  - llama.cpp
  - T3 Gemstone O1
  - Arduino UNO Q
  - ARM Cortex-A53
  - quantization
  - benchmarking
  - Vulkan
